    "q-113063": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113063",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{3t-15}{3{t}^{2}-30t+75}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we take out a factor of $3$ from the numerator and from the denominator, and then use the polynomial factorization ${t}^{2}-10t+25=(t-5)^{2}.$ Canceling out any common factors that appear in both the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3t-15}{3{t}^{2}-30t+75} & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3({t}^{2}-10t+25)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3(t-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(t-5)}{3(t-5)(t-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}\\cancel{(t-5)}}{\\cancel{3}\\cancel{(t-5)}(t-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
