    "q-113084": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113084",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$\\frac{5{h}^{2}-10h-15}{4{h}^{2}-4h-8}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{h}^{2}-10h-15}{4{h}^{2}-4h-8} & =\\frac{5({h}^{2}-2h-3)}{4({h}^{2}-h-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(h+1)(h-3)}{4(h-2)(h+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cancel{(h+1)}(h-3)}{4(h-2)\\cancel{(h+1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(h-3)}{4(h-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5h-15}{4h-8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
