    "q-150": {
      "dom_id": "step-q150",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "What is $\\frac{{y}^{2}-9}{{y}^{2}-6y+9}$ reduced to lowest terms?",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}-9}{{y}^{2}-6y+9} & =\\frac{(y+3)(y-3)}{(y-3)(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+3)\\cancel{(y-3)}}{(y-3)\\cancel{(y-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+3}{y-3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
